<!--
  A smaller branch in flower that ends inside its own frame.

  Generated, not drawn. This is the output of `lib/halftone.ts` in the
  su-clubfair website — a botanical field resolved through an ordered (Bayer)
  dither into a grid of marks, so the art stands on the same lattice as the
  Bitcount wordmark it sits behind. Regenerate from that module rather than
  editing here; every subpath is one dithered cell.

  Tone is carried by the density of marks, never by their opacity — that is what
  makes a dither read as ink rather than as a translucent sheet. Set alpha on the
  Image that draws this, not on the paths.

  **Split into 3 path elements on purpose.** The generator emits one path per
  size step, and for this piece that was a 41,000-character string. Android's
  binary XML holds each attribute in a string pool whose length field tops out
  around 32,767, so an over-long pathData comes back corrupted and the vector
  parser dies on whatever byte it lands in ("Unknown command for: R"). Splitting
  at subpath boundaries is free — the marks are independent — and every chunk is
  a valid path on its own. Keep chunks well under that ceiling.

  896 marks, 736x960 viewport.
-->
